","dish/cendol"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"],["Gepuk","dish/gepuk"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/2d/Cenil_Khas_Tulungagung.jpg/500px-Cenil_Khas_Tulungagung.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Robijuniarta","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cenil_Khas_Tulungagung.jpg"}},"ingredient/leeks":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/leeks","n":"Leeks","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["A leek is a biennial vegetable, a cultivar of Allium ampeloprasum, the broadleaf wild leek (syn. Allium porrum). The edible part of the plant is a bundle of leaf sheaths that is sometimes colloquially called a \"stem\" or \"stalk\"."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-leeks"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leeks"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Sephardic Jewish cuisine","cuisine/sephardic-jewish-cuisine",[["Fritas de prasa","dish/fritas-de-prasa"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Kosher salt","ingredient/kosher-salt"],["Matzo meal","ingredient/matzo-meal"],["Potatoes","ingredient/potatoes"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/63/Leek_on_white_background_-_0947.jpg/500px-Leek_on_white_background_-_0947.jpg","w":500,"h":734,"by":"Amada44","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leek_on_white_background_-_0947.jpg"}},"ingredient/edible-salt":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/edible-salt","n":"Edible salt","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 7 dishes across 15 cuisines","intro":[["Salt is a mineral composed primarily of sodium chloride (NaCl). When used in food, especially in granulated form, it is more formally called table salt. In the form of a natural crystalline mineral, salt is also known as rock salt or halite. Salt is essential for life in general (being the source of the essential dietary minerals sodium and chlorine), and saltiness is one of the basic human tastes. Salt is one of the oldest and most ubiquitous food seasonings, and is known to uniformly improve the taste perception of food. Salting, brining, and pickling are ancient and important methods of food preservation."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-edible-salt"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edible_salt"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":15,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Succotash","dish/succotash"]]],["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine",[["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]],["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",[["Tortang talong","dish/tortang-talong"]]],["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine",[["Greek salad","dish/greek-salad"]]],["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine",[["Naan","dish/naan"]]],["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine",[["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]],["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",[["Guacamole","dish/guacamole"]]],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao",[["Tortang talong","dish/tortang-talong"]]],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine",[["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]],["Swedish cuisine","cuisine/swedish-cuisine",[["Surströmming","dish/surstromming"]]],["Tex-Mex cuisine","cuisine/tex-mex-cuisine",[["Guacamole","dish/guacamole"]]],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine",[["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas",[["Tortang talong","dish/tortang-talong"]]],["Wampanoag foodways","cuisine/wampanoag-foodways",[["Succotash","dish/succotash"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Cucumber","ingredient/cucumber"],["Feta","ingredient/feta"],["Kalamata olive","ingredient/kalamata-olive"],["Olive","ingredient/olive"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Oregano","ingredient/oregano"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Avocado","ingredient/avocado"],["Jalapeño","ingredient/jalapeno"],["Lime (fruit)","ingredient/lime-fruit"],["Ghee","ingredient/ghee"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"]]}]},"ingredient/alkaline-noodles":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/alkaline-noodles","n":"Alkaline noodles","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Alkaline noodles or alkali noodles are a variation of noodles  traditional to Chinese cuisine with a much higher quantity of alkali than usual. The addition of alkali changes both the flavor and texture of the noodles, and makes them feel slippery in the mouth and on the fingers; they also develop a yellow color and are more elastic than ordinary noodles. Various flours such as ordinary all-purpose white flour, bread flour, and semolina flour can be used, with somewhat varying results. The yellow color is due to flavones that occur naturally in flour, which are normally colorless but turn yellow at alkaline pH."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-alkaline-noodles"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alkaline_noodles"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Hot dry noodles","dish/hot-dry-noodles"]]],["Hubei cuisine","cuisine/hubei-cuisine",[["Hot dry noodles","dish/hot-dry-noodles"]]],["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",[["Ramen","dish/ramen"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chili oil","ingredient/chili-oil"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Pickled carrots","ingredient/pickled-carrots"],["Sesame paste","ingredient/sesame-paste"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Japanese noodles","ingredient/japanese-noodles"],["Noodles","ingredient/noodles"],["Youmian","ingredient/youmian"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a8/Fresh_ramen_noodle_001.jpg/500px-Fresh_ramen_noodle_001.jpg","w":500,"h":364,"by":"Kropsoq","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fresh_ramen_noodle_001.jpg"}},"dish/iekei-ramen":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/iekei-ramen","n":"Iekei ramen","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Iekei ramen is a variety of ramen featuring a pork marrow and soy sauce broth and thick, straight noodles that was first invented in Yokohama by the ramen shop Yoshimura-ya in 1974.  In Canada, Iekei ramen or Yokohama Iekei ramen has become famous with Ramen Arashi located in Banff, Alberta, Canmore, Alberta and Victoria, British Columbia."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-iekei-ramen"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iekei_ramen"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","links":[["Bergh–Stoutenburgh House","dish/bergh-stoutenburgh-house"],["Chikuwa","dish/chikuwa"],["Curry bread","dish/curry-bread"],["Donburi","dish/donburi"],["Fukamushicha","dish/fukamushicha"],["Gyokuro","dish/gyokuro"],["Hitsumabushi","dish/hitsumabushi"],["Horumonyaki","dish/horumonyaki"],["Inago no tsukudani","dish/inago-no-tsukudani"],["Itamae","dish/itamae"],["Izakaya","dish/izakaya"],["Japanese cheesecake","dish/japanese-cheesecake"],["Japanese noodles","dish/japanese-noodles"],["Japanese restaurant","dish/japanese-restaurant"],["Japanese tea","dish/japanese-tea"],["Jingisukan","dish/jingisukan"],["Kaki furai","dish/kaki-furai"],["Kamaboko","dish/kamaboko"],["Kōji (food)","dish/koji-food"],["Kusa mochi","dish/kusa-mochi"],["Kushikatsu","dish/kushikatsu"],["List of Japanese restaurants","dish/list-of-japanese-restaurants"],["Makizushi","dish/makizushi"],["Miso","dish/miso"],["Miso soup","dish/miso-soup"],["Monjayaki","dish/monjayaki"],["Nikujaga","dish/nikujaga"],["Nimono","dish/nimono"],["Oden","dish/oden"],["Onigiri","dish/onigiri"],["Osechi","dish/osechi"],["Oyakodon","dish/oyakodon"],["Rainbow roll","dish/rainbow-roll"],["Ramen","dish/ramen"],["Ryōtei","dish/ryotei"],["Sashimi","dish/sashimi"],["Sencha","dish/sencha"],["Shizuoka oden","dish/shizuoka-oden"],["Sumiso","dish/sumiso"],["Sushi","dish/sushi"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/25/%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%A1%E3%83%B3%E3%81%A8%E3%83%A9%E3%82%A4%E3%82%B9_%E5%90%89%E6%9D%91%E5%AE%B6_2025%E5%B9%B42%E6%9C%8823%E6%97%A5%E3%81%AE%E6%A8%AA%E6%B5%9C_202502231704_IMG_9709.jpg/500px-%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%A1%E3%83%B3%E3%81%A8%E3%83%A9%E3%82%A4%E3%82%B9_%E5%90%89%E6%9D%91%E5%AE%B6_2025%E5%B9%B42%E6%9C%8823%E6%97%A5%E3%81%AE%E6%A8%AA%E6%B5%9C_202502231704_IMG_9709.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"ウィ貴公子","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://c